# Transport Modes

Choosing the right transport depends on the network environment and operational constraints.

## Choosing a Transport

Use **TCP (WebSockets)** when you need to traverse an HTTP proxy, blend in with HTTPS traffic for DPI evasion, or front through a CDN. WebSocket is also faster on clean, low-latency networks (same data centre, local LAN) where packet loss is negligible.

Use **UDP (QUIC)** for most pen test scenarios. QUIC's per-stream loss recovery prevents a single dropped packet from stalling the entire tunnel. Under real-world conditions (packet loss above 0.5% and latency above 20 ms), WebSocket throughput collapses while QUIC maintains usable speeds. See [Benchmarks](/docs/benchmarks) for the full data.

## UDP (QUIC)

The default transport. Network conditions in penetration testing environments are rarely predictable. QUIC handles this better than TCP. Per-stream loss recovery means a dropped packet stalls only that connection, not the entire tunnel. Native stream multiplexing and built-in TLS 1.3. Append `/udp` to the address, or omit the suffix entirely.

{% codeblock code="wallhack entry --listen :443/udp" /%}

## TCP (WebSockets)

Traffic is wrapped in WebSockets and will appear as standard HTTPS to firewalls and Deep Packet Inspection (DPI) tools. Append `/tcp` to the address.

{% codeblock code="wallhack entry --listen :443/tcp" /%}

When an explicit HTTP or SOCKS5 proxy is required, set the standard environment variables before starting the exit node. Both HTTP CONNECT and SOCKS5 (`socks5://`) schemes are supported.

```bash
export HTTPS_PROXY=http://proxy.corp.internal:8080
wallhack exit --connect 192.168.1.5:443/tcp
```

`NO_PROXY` is also respected for comma-separated host exclusions.

### CDN Fronting

Traffic can be proxied through a CDN worker such as a Cloudflare Worker. The traffic legitimately terminates at the CDN's infrastructure, making it significantly harder to attribute or block.

{% codeblock code="wallhack entry --listen :443/tcp --cert cert.pem --key key.pem" /%}
